pathological_tests.py is copied byte for byte. cmark states its
pathological cases only as this Python generator: each input is a Python
expression, and one, "reference collisions", is the value of the function
hash_collisions(). pathological_test.go reads the file and evaluates the
inputs as data; see its comment for how, and for the one function it
mirrors. Updating the file is a deliberate change: take a new commit, copy
both files again, and update this note.
